(6647366, 991787, 20799, '<td valign="top">Tomato is a little wrinkled - is it the same model from the Weston challenge? :)<br/>Just a thought remembering your shots with the TS lens... maybe it would have been interesting to close in on the tomato and add some distortion, could go well with the clown suit :). Nevertheless, well done, congrats on the ribbon! <br/></td>', 'Tomato is a little wrinkled - is it the same model from the Weston challenge? :)Just a thought remembering your shots with the TS lens... maybe it would have been interesting to close in on the tomato and add some distortion, could go well with the clown suit :). Nevertheless, well done, congrats on the ribbon! ', '2012-01-17 03:02:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647400, 991725, 114233, '<td valign="top">Another top 10! Well done!<br/>Lovely separation with the DOF. Set up is nice with the clothes and snake etc. Next time use a more dangerous snake like a Gaboon adder or a Rhinoceros viper to add more drama... call me if you need them soon :-)</td>', 'Another top 10! Well done!Lovely separation with the DOF. Set up is nice with the clothes and snake etc. Next time use a more dangerous snake like a Gaboon adder or a Rhinoceros viper to add more drama... call me if you need them soon :-)', '2012-01-17 05:05:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647407, 991787, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tome:</b></div><hr/><i> Tomato is a little wrinkled - is it the same model from the Weston challenge? :)<br/>Just a thought remembering your shots with the TS lens... maybe it would have been interesting to close in on the tomato and add some distortion, could go well with the clown suit :). Nevertheless, well done, congrats on the ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment! It is hard for me to use my TS lens in my home studio, since its focal length is 17mm: my back wall is too narrow, unless I put the lens very close to it. Yes, I know, I need a bigger studio ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by tome: Tomato is a little wrinkled - is it the same model from the Weston challenge? :)Just a thought remembering your shots with the TS lens... maybe it would have been interesting to close in on the tomato and add some distortion, could go well with the clown suit :). Nevertheless, well done, congrats on the ribbon!   Thanks for your comment! It is hard for me to use my TS lens in my home studio, since its focal length is 17mm: my back wall is too narrow, unless I put the lens very close to it. Yes, I know, I need a bigger studio ;-)', '2012-01-17 05:45:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647426, 991796, 93565, '<td valign="top">Ha! Man, I think this one is kinda cool... bummer it scored so low. The "floating" writing is an interesting effect.</td>', 'Ha! Man, I think this one is kinda cool... bummer it scored so low. The "floating" writing is an interesting effect.', '2012-01-17 07:42:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647428, 991918, 93565, '<td valign="top">Awwww no comments!<br/> <br/>I''m curious as to what the butterfly like ghosting is top right? Any ideas? Intentional or no?</td>', 'Awwww no comments! I''m curious as to what the butterfly like ghosting is top right? Any ideas? Intentional or no?', '2012-01-17 07:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647429, 991920, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''d say some work with the lighting would''ve been best on this one-<br/>Since the scale of things is so small here, it wouldn''t be too hard to use a sheet of paper relatively low above them reflecting a flash or the light from some constant light source, like a halogen worklamp. Just make sure you lower your ambient light so that you don''t have multiple color temperatures.<br/>Placing the paper above it would make the lighting more even and soft because the relative size of the source is large. This way, they wouldn''t cast so much of a shadow.</td>', 'I''d say some work with the lighting would''ve been best on this one-Since the scale of things is so small here, it wouldn''t be too hard to use a sheet of paper relatively low above them reflecting a flash or the light from some constant light source, like a halogen worklamp. Just make sure you lower your ambient light so that you don''t have multiple color temperatures.Placing the paper above it would make the lighting more even and soft because the relative size of the source is large. This way, they wouldn''t cast so much of a shadow.', '2012-01-17 07:52:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647503, 991796, 141273, '<td valign="top">No, i don''t</td>', 'No, i don''t', '2012-01-17 11:00:37.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6647611, 991134, 68504, '<td valign="top">how''d I miss this? bittersweet January.</td>', 'how''d I miss this? bittersweet January.', '2012-01-17 13:00:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6647621, 991874, 30364, '<td valign="top">I''m still dismayed.  The ''foreign culture'' excuse of unawareness of the iconic redness of a Radio Flyer wagon is no excuse at all.  Everyone here has by definition a computer, and thus a Google or equivalent.  DPC challenges only ever present the voter with a tiny handful of unmistakably ambitious images to consider.  It takes only a moment for the culturally unaware to inform themselves, and thereby be equipped to make an informed judgement.  Lack of awareness is forgivable in an artist, but lack of curiosity is not. The real magic is very often in the oddball images that you don''t initially comprehend.</td>', 'I''m still dismayed.  The ''foreign culture'' excuse of unawareness of the iconic redness of a Radio Flyer wagon is no excuse at all.  Everyone here has by definition a computer, and thus a Google or equivalent.  DPC challenges only ever present the voter with a tiny handful of unmistakably ambitious images to consider.  It takes only a moment for the culturally unaware to inform themselves, and thereby be equipped to make an informed judgement.  Lack of awareness is forgivable in an artist, but lack of curiosity is not. The real magic is very often in the oddball images that you don''t initially comprehend.', '2012-01-17 13:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
