(6651969, 990919, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First impression: Love the bokeh and the details here.<br/> <br/>Artistic: This is great use of shallow dof, and the red definitely pops without being too much.  The only thing I''m personally not fond of is the pedal showing at the bottom; the pedal arm (or whatever it''s called :-) just intrudes a little too much, especially as it''s light in colour.<br/> <br/>Technical: Apart from the minor nitpick with the bottom pedal, there''s not much else to find fault with.  Composition is simple, the ambient lighting adds a nice feel to the shot and the details of the locking mechanism are perfectly rendered. The swirly blue/green bg adds a slightly surreal edge, almost a zoomblur or lensbaby effect.<br/> <br/>Overall: Gave you a 7 during voting and glad I did, but if it were possible to have shot it without that crank arm and pedal lower or out of frame, may have got you an 8.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First impression: Love the bokeh and the details here. Artistic: This is great use of shallow dof, and the red definitely pops without being too much.  The only thing I''m personally not fond of is the pedal showing at the bottom; the pedal arm (or whatever it''s called :-) just intrudes a little too much, especially as it''s light in colour. Technical: Apart from the minor nitpick with the bottom pedal, there''s not much else to find fault with.  Composition is simple, the ambient lighting adds a nice feel to the shot and the details of the locking mechanism are perfectly rendered. The swirly blue/green bg adds a slightly surreal edge, almost a zoomblur or lensbaby effect. Overall: Gave you a 7 during voting and glad I did, but if it were possible to have shot it without that crank arm and pedal lower or out of frame, may have got you an 8. Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-01-22 15:30:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6652169, 991415, 132996, '<td valign="top">I like this image. I think you definitely stepped out of the box in finding a unique subject for the challenge. Unfortunately it didn''t pay off too well in the challenge. :\<br/> <br/>My impression is that the ball is too centered (or even not enough centered) and too small in the frame to generate the interest you want. I do like the texture that the mosaic generates in your background, but there''s just something missing from the image. Maybe it''s a story...or a general direction. When I look at it, my eyes aren''t directed anywhere. In fact, the arms of Jesus tend to draw my eyes out the top of the image. I think a harder look at the subject would generate a more compelling image.</td>', 'I like this image. I think you definitely stepped out of the box in finding a unique subject for the challenge. Unfortunately it didn''t pay off too well in the challenge. :\ My impression is that the ball is too centered (or even not enough centered) and too small in the frame to generate the interest you want. I do like the texture that the mosaic generates in your background, but there''s just something missing from the image. Maybe it''s a story...or a general direction. When I look at it, my eyes aren''t directed anywhere. In fact, the arms of Jesus tend to draw my eyes out the top of the image. I think a harder look at the subject would generate a more compelling image.', '2012-01-22 20:56:23.000000', NULL, 0),
